"content_hash":"1a1c68d5fda575f0f5732280feacd5f70a72b52f09d1b63dc8ffc3af171bf264","event_uuid":"f8038e58-60a3-4166-9e33-6c2c9dbae93f","position":{"commit_sha":"a8f5f7c636183b37b9af2e204b0fe20f390ad92b","position":"1785867628063282001-f8038e58-60a3-4166-9e33-6c2c9dbae93f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"618fc5f34ba39a81607342566a84a1a763d2b5d9a939444f6af8eab3ea529713","event_uuid":"d5883dc5-5497-42cf-a72c-296be13398de","position":{"commit_sha":"99c5cb5b09f68857a46416502c44826f12e7cd1a","position":"1785867987496710001-d5883dc5-5497-42cf-a72c-296be13398de"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix pushed for review as Gerrit change 1384: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1384\n\nApproach (operator-approved options a + c):\n- (a) Token moved OUT of the URL: both /webhook and /rerun now read the secret from the X-Rebar-Token HTTP header (preferred), which uvicorn's access log does not record. Legacy ?token= query param still accepted for backward-compat until Gerrit's webhooks.config is re-pushed. webhooks.config updated to send the token via 'header = X-Rebar-Token: __BOT_TOKEN__' instead of the URL.\n- (c) Belt-and-suspenders: install_access_log_redaction() attaches TokenRedactingFilter to the uvicorn.access logger, scrubbing token=<value> from any request line before stderr/journald while preserving route + status for observability greps.\n- Runbook infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md /rerun recipe rewritten to use -H 'X-Rebar-Token' (no URL token) with a rotation note.\n\nFiles changed: src/rebar/review_bot/app.py, src/rebar/review_bot/config.py, tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_redaction.py (new), infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md, infra/gerrit/webhooks.config.\n\nTests: 7 new (redaction filter scrubs sentinel query token while keeping route/status; header-authed /rerun logs no sentinel; header auth works for both endpoints; missing/wrong tokens still 401; query backward-compat still authenticates). Full review-bot suite 136 passed. make lint + make typecheck clean. Both endpoints keep the token out of the request line via the header; redaction filter installed as backstop.\n\nREMINDER: this code fix MUST LAND (Verified +1, merged) BEFORE the operator rotates GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN -- otherwise the newly rotated token is logged the moment it is first used through any legacy query-string caller. Rotation is operator-owned and tracked separately. Not closing this ticket: closing needs Verified +1 (green CI) and the rotation must follow the merge.","timestamp":1785867987496710001}],"created_at":1785805083008038001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"34916eff-1abd-4393-abec-302015caf05e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"694a-ff0c-7173-4f65"},{"link_uuid":"992a90d8-11c0-49db-9ee1-871607e7e423","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"36db-8191-2150-4ba5"}],"description":"# The shared webhook/rerun secret is written to journald in every access-log line\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe review-bot receiver is a uvicorn app, and uvicorn's default access log records the full\nrequest line INCLUDING THE QUERY STRING. Both authenticated endpoints take their secret as a\nQUERY PARAMETER (`?token=...`), so every request writes the secret to stderr -> journald in\nclear text:\n\n    INFO:  127.0.0.1:34184 - \"POST /rerun?token=<the actual secret>&change=1323 HTTP/1.1\" 202 Accepted\n    INFO:  172.21.0.4:33070 - \"POST /webhook?token=<the actual secret> HTTP/1.1\" 202 Accepted\n\nObserved directly in the production container's journal (`journalctl CONTAINER_NAME=compose-review-bot-1`).\n\n## Why it matters\n\n* **The secret is the auth for both endpoints.** `config.py:239` is\n  `webhook_token = os.environ.get(\"WEBHOOK_TOKEN\", \"\").strip() or bot_token`, and this\n  container sets no `WEBHOOK_TOKEN`, so the webhook token IS `GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN` — the\n  review bot's Gerrit credential. Anything that can read the journal therefore learns a\n  credential that can both drive reviews AND act as the bot against Gerrit.\n* **The blast radius is wider than the box.** journald content flows into anything that reads\n  it: `infra/scripts/observability.sh` greps the same journal, operators paste log excerpts into\n  tickets and chat, and any future log-shipping would carry the secret off-host. It also means\n  the secret cannot be treated as unexposed after any incident that involved sharing logs.\n* **It is a fail-open exposure, not a fail-closed one:** nothing errors, nothing alarms, and the\n  endpoint keeps working — so there is no signal that would ever surface it.\n\nDISCOVERED the hard way: an agent grepping the journal for `/rerun` activity while working\n[rebar:eb6e-f43a-e86b-443a] surfaced the token into a session transcript. That is the failure mode\n— the secret is sitting in the most-grepped log on the box.\n\n**This ticket does not fix the exposure that already happened.** The token in the journal (and\nanywhere journal excerpts have been shared) must be treated as compromised and ROTATED\nindependently of the code fix. Rotation alone is also not sufficient: without the fix, the new\ntoken is logged the moment it is first used.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/app.py` — the `/webhook` and `/rerun` handlers and/or the uvicorn\n  logging configuration (`configure_logging`).\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot` — the `uvicorn` invocation, if the access-log format or\n  its disabling belongs there.\n- `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` — the `/rerun` recipe currently instructs the operator to\n  put the token in a URL, which is what puts it in the log; and a rotation note.\n\n## Approach (options, with the tradeoff stated)\n\n1. **Move the secret out of the query string** — accept it as a header (e.g. `X-Rebar-Token`) or\n   in the POST body. Cleanest: access logs record the request line, not headers. But\n   `/webhook` is called BY GERRIT, so the Gerrit-side webhook configuration must be able to\n   send it — check what the `webhook` plugin supports before assuming a header is expressible.\n   `/rerun` is operator-driven and can move to a header immediately regardless.\n2. **Scrub the access log** — install a uvicorn log filter that redacts `token=[^&]*`. Keeps the\n   URL shape, protects the value, and covers BOTH endpoints even if Gerrit cannot send a header.\n   Weaker in principle (the secret still transits a URL, so it can leak via any other component\n   that logs URLs) but it is the only option that works without a Gerrit-side change.\n3. Do both: header for `/rerun`, redaction filter as the backstop for `/webhook`.\n\nDo NOT simply disable the access log — it is load-bearing for debugging and for the\n`observability.sh` greps.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe oracle must assert on the EMITTED LOG LINE, not on the handler's behaviour, because the\nhandler is already correct — it is the logging that leaks:\n\n- drive a request carrying a known sentinel token through the app with `caplog` (or a captured\n  uvicorn handler) and assert the sentinel does NOT appear in any emitted record, while the\n  route and status DO;\n- verify RED by reverting the fix and observing the sentinel reappear;\n- if a header is adopted, a second test that a query-string token is REJECTED (or at least not\n  logged), so the old path cannot quietly persist.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the webhook/rerun secret no longer appears in any log record the receiver emits, proven by\n      a test that asserts on the emitted log line with a sentinel value and is verified RED by\n      reverting the fix.\n- [ ] the mechanism is stated in the code where the choice is made (header vs redaction filter),\n      including WHY — so a future change does not reintroduce the query-string form as a\n      convenience.\n- [ ] `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md`'s `/rerun` recipe no longer instructs the operator to\n      put the token in a URL, and carries a note that the previous token must be treated as\n      compromised and rotated.\n- [ ] the access log still records route and status for both endpoints (the observability greps\n      and debugging value are not sacrificed to fix this).\n- [ ] ROTATION IS TRACKED SEPARATELY AND EXPLICITLY: the currently-logged token is rotated, and\n      that rotation is recorded as done rather than assumed, since the code fix does not\n      un-leak what is already in journald.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","reason":"accept token via X-Rebar-Token header; keep query fallback but out of preferred path"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/config.py","reason":"install uvicorn access-log token redaction filter"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_redaction.py","reason":"new tests: token absent from log line; redaction filter scrubs query token"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"header-based /rerun recipe + rotation note"},{"path":"infra/gerrit/webhooks.config","reason":"send token via header instead of URL"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","36db-8191-2150-4ba5"],["relates_to","694a-ff0c-7173-4f65"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2d9a9b80-1aec-41f6-9faf-0cc2b3bb042b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"66af-64be-786c-474f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Review-bot logs the webhook token in plaintext on every /webhook and /rerun request","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["12e7eac4-4ba9-4d91-bc4e-97fd546c82ca","35093408-69aa-466e-9ab7-9bea7b3015e8","d9d40510-4a4e-47af-be31-076bdb8155e3","0343c62b-34ba-41e9-88f4-b861e462b81f","d6140fba-4d10-4b41-84fd-09bbcc2616ce","fc15d811-2e4b-4bf1-aca9-20f81e125ddb","2d9a9b80-1aec-41f6-9faf-0cc2b3bb042b","96f98963-a8dd-4faa-9985-839ab6bbe656","f8038e58-60a3-4166-9e33-6c2c9dbae93f","d5883dc5-5497-42cf-a72c-296be13398de","34916eff-1abd-4393-abec-302015caf05e","992a90d8-11c0-49db-9ee1-871607e7e423"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785871252505018690,"uuid":"92d6bd80-e87b-41f3-9de6-b3f535a4e355"}